  "query_preview": "../Sunday through Tuesday/...For Sunday, onshore flow \nmay strengthen a bit as a marine air mass becomes more fully \nestablished. As a result, there will probably be a few more areas \nof light rain and drizzle, particularly from Cape Edgecumbe \nnorthward. Under increased cloudiness, high temperatures will also\nbe somewhat cooler.\n\nThe pattern turns more active by Labor Day as the next organized \nlow pressure system begins to impact the area. The Canadian model \nstill wants to break down the ridge of high pressure soonest, but \nit has come closer in timing with the GFS and ECMWF. We have \nhigher confidence that rain chances increase for much of the \nregion after about 12Z-18Z Monday, except over the southeast. This\nwetter and cooler pattern will continue into Tuesday. Although it\nis still a bit early to discuss rainfall amounts for Mon-Tue, \nlatest guidance suggests around 2 inches for the northeast Gulf \ncoast to about 0.75\" in the central panhandle with lighter amounts\nfarther south.",
